questions.question:
A team grades small Python submissions inside the worker process itself and adds a heartbeat:

const heartbeat = setInterval(() => {
  sqs.send(new ChangeMessageVisibilityCommand({ QueueUrl, ReceiptHandle: msg.ReceiptHandle, VisibilityTimeout: 60 }))
    .then(() => logger.info("heartbeat", msg.MessageId));
}, 20_000);
try {
  const result = runTestsSync(submission);   // synchronous, CPU-bound, up to 70 s
  await saveResult(result);
  await deleteMessage(msg);
} finally {
  clearInterval(heartbeat);
}

Logs for a 70-second run: "received" at 0 s, "graded" at 70 s, no "heartbeat" line in between.

Statement: "Because the worker calls ChangeMessageVisibility every 20 seconds, a 70-second run can no longer be received by a second worker."
